# Avoid Unnecessary Comments

Do not add comments that narrate, restate, or label what the code obviously does. Comments should only explain non-obvious **intent**, **trade-offs**, or **constraints** that the code itself cannot convey.

## Don't write these

- Section labels (`// Imports`, `// State`, `// Helpers`)
- Step narration (`// Increment counter`, `// Return result`, `// Loop through items`)
- Restating signatures (`// Function that fetches user`)
- Change-log comments (`// Updated to use new API`, `// Fixed bug here`)
- Obvious type/value comments (`// string`, `// true`)

## Do write these

- Why a non-obvious choice was made
- Workarounds tied to external constraints (browser quirks, library bugs) — link/cite the cause
- Invariants the code relies on but doesn't express
- TODOs with concrete context

## Examples

```ts
// ❌ BAD
// Increment count
count += 1;

// Fetch the user
const user = await fetchUser(id);

// Loop through items
for (const item of items) { ... }
```

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
// Safari ignores `preventDefault` on passive listeners; force non-passive here.
el.addEventListener("touchmove", onMove, { passive: false });

// LinkedIn rate-limits at ~100 req/min per IP — keep batch size below this.
const BATCH_SIZE = 80;
```

If you'd delete the comment and the code still reads clearly, the comment shouldn't exist.
